(-2)^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392340 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392340 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392340 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392340 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392340 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8a18aba-5bf5-5598-9a5a-e92c825d1e00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392340 #edb/ref 1074 "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}v=\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=\\frac{11}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{11}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+11[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392341 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "622b7cda-79c9-5c80-96ea-60d2acfa05fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392342 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392342 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392342 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3e41f35-f9a3-51af-aed3-cadc7a55cbe9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392343 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392343 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392343 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c12aa19b-3eaf-56cc-9bcd-1fd70423d422" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392344 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]"